# PROVE — toward radius-2 charging

## GATE

Copied `ref/source_defect_round7.py` to `scratch/` unmodified and ran it. Reproduced **exactly**: prescribed_cases 108, posthoc_cases 47, positive_lift_cases 5, min_M_over_L_positive `17/8`, generic_counterexample_output_over_input `10/9` (~12 s, status PASS). Gate OK; all numbers below are new.

Result headline: **not proved** (partial). Genuine proved structural core + exact mechanism anatomy + four first-class negative results that kill the natural proof routes. One clean minimal gap isolated.

## 1. Combinatorial opening of L_k (formula + verification count)

[PROOF] Let `W_{m,k} = {w ∈ {0,1}^m : w_0 = 1, |w| = k}` (odd starts `< 2^m` biject with these; `|W| = n_k = binom(m-1,k-1)`). For `w` with start `h_w` and endpoint `e_w = H^m(h_w)`, `z_w = e_w mod N`, `N = 2^{s+1}`:
`P_k(z) = #{w ∈ W_{m,k} : z_w = z}`, hence `C_k(d) = #{(w,w′) ∈ W² : z_{w′} − z_w = d}`,
`L_k = q·(N⁺_k − N⁻_k)/n_k` with `N⁺_k, N⁻_k` ordered endpoint-pair counts at shifts `3^k`, `3^k+q`.
[EXACT COMPUTATION] Pair-count form == operator form on **51 cases** (m = 2..12, s ≤ 6), 0 failures; histogram-product count == brute ordered-pair count each time. R-affine (`e_w·2^m = 3^k h_w + B_w`, recursive `B`) + R-odd-offset verified for **every** word at m = 4, 6, 8 (8+32+128 words); R-mass verified throughout. (Finite checks, not a theorem.)

## 2. Combinatorial opening of M_j (same)

[PROOF] Each `w ∈ W_{m,k}` lifts to the pair `(x_w, x_w + 3^k)` of opposite parity; the even member feeds `E_k[H(y)]`, the odd feeds `O_k[H(y)]`. So `E_k, O_k` are exact word-count histograms and `M_j = J_s(n_{j-1}E_j − n_jO_{j−1})/[n_jn_{j−1}(n_j+n_{j−1})]` is a weighted square norm of a word-mismatch vector.
[EXACT COMPUTATION] Direct lifted-start enumeration (no transfer operators) == `Eop/Oop` output on the same **51 cases**, 0 failures — second implementation. Plus: [PROOF] parent identity `P_{m,k,s+1} = E^par(Q_k) + O^par(Q_{k−1})`, `Q_j = P_{m−1,j,s+2}`, parent-weight shifts — verified on **40 cases**, 0 failures. Consequence [PROOF]: `L_k` touches parents `{Q_k, Q_{k−1}}`, `M_j` touches `{Q_j, Q_{j−1}, Q_{j−2}}`; overlap ⟺ `j ∈ [k−1, k+2]`. **Radius 2 is exactly the parent-sharing horizon** — this is why reach stops at 2: beyond it the parent variables are disjoint, so no parent-local argument can couple them. (Index logic given the verified identity.)

## 3. Anatomy of the radius-1 failures (why locality breaks, exactly)

[EXACT COMPUTATION] Full 210-row grid (m = 2..24, s ≤ min(12, m−1)), self-contained reimplementation: **radius-2 violations 0; natural-radius-1 (`[a,b+1]`) violations exactly 27** — count and all values match the lead's data; second independent implementation (lifted starts) reproduces **27/27 exact gap strings** and r2 = 0 on all 9 host cells. (Tables are finite evidence, not a theorem.)
Headline row `(18,2)[14,14]`: demand `3/35`, natural supply `M₁₄+M₁₅ = 4033/69615`, gap `1934/69615` — exact match. Mechanism, derived not guessed: `P₁₄` mod 8 is a near-flat sea (`[306,305,295,298,294,302,286,294]`, mass 2380); lift is a 51-pair ripple (`C(c)−C(c+q) = 51` of ~5.6M pairs); the natural merges starve because `E₁₄/n₁₄ ≈ O₁₃/n₁₃` bin-wise (first bins exactly equal, `30/119`), so `M₁₄` is tiny; the deficit is paid ~4× over by `M₁₃` and ~80× over by `M₁₆`, whose low-mass spiky inputs (`E₁₆ = [29,28,37,42]`) carry huge slack. Parent split at the 7 failing singletons: the **AB cross term** (between the `Q_k` even-lift and `Q_{k−1}` odd-lift pieces) dominates in 4/7. Minimality is two-sided [EXACT COMPUTATION]: `(23,2)[11,11]` needs the left outer (right `M₁₃` insufficient) while `(20,3)[13,16]` needs the right outer (left `M₁₂` insufficient) — neither one-sided extension works globally.

## 4. Proof attempt (a): direct interval bound — result

[FAIL] with witnesses. Termwise charging is dead: `AB_k⁺ ≤ window` fails at `(18,2,7)` (gap `1306483/3063060`) — pieces cancel (`L₇ < 0` there), so no per-piece domination can work. `AA_k⁺ ≤ M_{k+1}+M_{k+2}` fails twice on the big grid (first `(23,2,10)`); both one-sided singleton chargings fail once each (above). Survivor (pattern only, [DIAGNOSTIC], 210-grid/3012 cases): `BB_k⁺ ≤ M_{k−1}+M_k+M_{k+1}` holds — the E/O gauge asymmetry is real but unproved. No injection was found; (a) is blocked at piece cancellation.

## 5. Proof attempt (b): minimal violating interval — result

[PROOF] (pure logic) A minimal r2-violating interval has `L_a, L_b > 0` at both endpoints — verified non-vacuously on the dead-end witnesses (minimal violators `(2,2)` and `(2,3)`, endpoints strictly positive). Note w2's minimal violator has length 2: the interval form is strictly stronger than singleton form. The contradiction step stalls: assuming violation, R-cap gives only `L_a ≤ q·cap` ([PROOF] one-line bound, `0 ≤ C(d) ≤ cap·n`; **3236 checks, 0 failures**), which is vacuous at small s (`(18,2,14)`: bound 1224 vs actual `3/35`) though nearly tight at small mass (`(4,2,2)`: ratio 2/3). No lower bound on outer merges follows from R-affine + R-odd-offset, which constrain words individually but not pairs jointly. (b) reduces to the gap below.

## 6. THE SMALLEST REMAINING GAP (exact statement, exact quantifiers, finite object)

[CONJECTURE] (Outer-pay, subset form.) For all integers `m ≥ 3`, `s ≥ 1`, all `1 ≤ a ≤ b ≤ m`, all `S ⊆ [a,b]`: `Σ_{k∈S} L_k ≤ Σ_{j=max(a−1,2)}^{min(b+2,m)} M_j`, where all quantities are the explicit word-count rational functions above evaluated on parent vectors `(Q_{k−3},…,Q_{k+2})` (precision `s+2`) satisfying R-mass, R-support, R-cap, R-odd-offset. Each instance is finite (bounded integer vectors + binomial weights); the family is infinite over `(m,s)` with `m`-dependent weight ratios — uniformity in `m` is the entire remaining difficulty. Singleton form alone is insufficient (w2 `[2,3]`).

## 7. Consistency check against the four dead-end witnesses

[EXACT COMPUTATION] Generic identities (shift-L, square-M) **hold** on witnesses 1–2, as they must (reachability-free). Radius-2 charging **fails** on both (4 viols w1, e.g. `[1,2]` gap `4/3`; 6 viols w2), as it must. Hypothesis accounting: w1 respects masses/caps but breaks **real supports** (k=2: `{0,7}` vs real `{2,4}`); w2 respects supports/masses but breaks **real caps** (k=2: 3 vs 1; k=4: 3 vs 1). Items 3–4 (pointwise-k, radius-1 failures) are true facts of the real source that any valid derivation must accommodate — mine does (never claims them). So a sound proof must use supports AND caps; mine invokes both.

## 8. Does the argument use the max-entry cap? Where?

Yes — necessarily (§7: without it, dead-end 2 is a counterexample to every step). Cap enters at exactly two places: the universal lift bound `|L_k| ≤ q·cap_k` (step toward (b)) and the exclusion of piled adversarial families from the gap's quantifier domain (§6). Honest caveat [DIAGNOSTIC]: at small s the cap bound is vacuous, so the cap does its real work by shaping the admissible set, not by crude counting — the supcap DP results (positive minima) are consistent with this but cover only 4 cells.

